:name: oveRTOS CMocka suite on NuttX/STM32F746 — heap mode
:description: Boot the oveRTOS test firmware on NuttX's stm32f746g-disco target under Renode's stm32f7_discovery-bb platform; capture stdout via USART1.

using sysbus

$bin?=@output/tests/renode-stm32f746-nuttx/nuttx/nuttx

mach create "stm32f746"
machine LoadPlatformDescription @platforms/boards/stm32f7_discovery-bb.repl

sysbus LoadELF $bin

# NuttX's stm32f746g-disco:nsh uses USART1 as the serial console
# (CONFIG_USART1_SERIAL_CONSOLE).  Renode's STM32F7_USART model accepts
# the byte writes — tap its TX into a file backend so the harness can
# parse the CMocka summary post-run.
$uart_out?=@/tmp/renode-stm32f746-nuttx.uart
sysbus.usart1 CreateFileBackend $uart_out true
showAnalyzer sysbus.usart1

$rlog?=@/tmp/renode-stm32f746-nuttx.renode.log
logFile $rlog

# Same budget rationale as the Zephyr sibling — NuttX's STM32F7 boot
# is slower under Renode than mps2-an500's.
# NuttX prints the test summary at ~0.7s of simulated time; 5s gives
# margin without risking the 300s wall-clock harness ceiling.
emulation RunFor "00:00:05"
